CHAPTER VI

COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION

Article 27

1. The community may participate in assisting efforts to prevent and handle victims of gender-based violence and violence against children.
2. Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in the form of:
a. providing information and/or reporting any violence that comes to their knowledge;
b. providing protection for victims;
c. providing emergency assistance;
d. providing advocacy to victims and or the community regarding the handling of gender-based violence and violence against children;
e. assisting in the process of submitting applications for protection orders; and
f. assisting in the process of repatriation and social reintegration.
3. Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be carried out by individuals, social community institutions, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, the private sector, and mass media.

Article 17

Increasing Community Participation as referred to in Article 9 letter h is carried out by:
a. fostering community awareness of cases of gender-based violence and children;
b. encouraging the community to actively participate in providing information and reporting gender-based violence and children;
c. fostering local wisdom in handling gender-based violence and children;
d. organizing strengthening of community groups in handling gender-based violence and children; and
e. disseminating information about laws and regulations related to gender-based violence and children.

